    "md5": "b80e3c88d8331f4203381c230e6e53dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "A new economic transformation at the rural level can be brought about by encouraging small and medium-scale entrepreneurs, creating new economic opportunities for rural people, and developing the technical, vocational and linguistic skills required for the modern job market.\n\n2.5 Stability and Continuity of the Energy\n\nMarkets\n\n2.6 Strengthening Resilience to Climate Disasters\n\nIt is important to follow standards capable of withstanding future disasters, early warnings and proper maintenance plans. Along with this, food supply chains, storage, public transport and the mechanisms for distributing essential goods must be strengthened. The continuity of services such as essential communication facilities and electricity must be ensured. Although the risks arising from natural disasters that may occur in the future cannot be completely eliminated, our objective is to significantly minimize the resulting paralysis of economic activities and the pressure on people's lives.\n\n2.7 Modernizing the Government Machinery\n\nIt is essential to build an efficient Government machinery that provides a quality service to the people, facilitates investment and production activities, and is accountable to the law and transparent. Modernizing public financial management, State-owned Enterprise and asset management, tax administration and the procurement process are essential elements of this. Minimizing corruption and unnecessary administrative delays, while strengthening the rule of law and accountability, is equally important to enhance public trust and to safeguard public resources.\n\n3. Medium-Term Macroeconomic and Fiscal\n\nPath"
