    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, we expect to maintain public investment at a level exceeding 4 per cent of GDP from 2027 onwards. In 2027, a Capital Expenditure of Rs. 2,000 billion has been allocated, amounting to total public investment of 5.12 per cent of GDP, comprising 4.48 per cent through the Budget and 0.64 per cent through the Supplementary Estimate for Ditwah.\n\nTherefore, the Cabinet of Ministers has appointed a committee headed by the Deputy Minister of Finance and Planning to examine and submit a report on the suitability of entering into another programme after the successful completion of the current IMF programme, and on what type of programme it should be.\n\nFor social justice and the protection of the people, targeted social protection programmes will be further strengthened to protect low-income and vulnerable households who face the highest risk in the face of economic and natural disasters.\n\nHon. Speaker, our people made exceptional sacrifices and endured great hardships for this economic stabilization. We must all pay our respect to them. Doing justice to these sacrifices means achieving a rapid turn from economic stabilization towards transformation. To that end, I present to this honourable House the Budget Proposals for the year 2027.\n\nBuilding the Essential Foundations for Economic Transformation\n\n4. Strengthening the Legal Framework"
