    "chunk_text": "improving the infrastructure of institutions belonging to the technical education and training sector, including the German Technical Training Institute and the Automobile Engineering Training Institute.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,500 million has been allocated for the year\n\n2027 for the project costing Rs. 6,000 million to modernize 25 selected Technical Colleges in 25 districts.\n\n9. Towards an Economic Transformation\n\nthrough Research, Development and Innovation\n\nHon. Speaker, the National Council for Research and Development has been established for policy guidance in the field of science and technology and for directing and coordinating research activities. Through this, its main function is to identify all national research - science, technology, engineering, agriculture, medicine - and to work by giving priority to research that contributes to the production economy. This will not be limited to science and technology activities, but will also undertake research relating to defence and social welfare activities.\n\nThrough this,\n\n\u2022 Monitoring and regulating research and development\n\nactivities carried out by the public as well as the private sector.\n\n\u2022 Directing research in a manner that contributes to\n\nnational development goals and economic growth.\n\n\u2022 Developing the capabilities of local researchers\n\nand supporting advanced research of international standard.\n\n\u2022 Transforming the results of research carried out in\n\nlaboratories and universities into products or services useful to society and the industrial sector.\n\n\u2022 Preparing national research and development policies\n\nto suit the future needs of the country.\n\n\u2022 Taking new technologies discovered through research to commercialization and integrating them into the country's economy."
