    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Rs. 102 million has been allocated for an alternative care structure focused on vulnerable children and children who have lost their parents due to disasters.\n\n\u2022 A Disability Inclusion Focal Point will be established in every Ministry, department and major public institution for the community of persons with disabilities.\n\n\u2022 The establishment of accessible digital public services will be made mandatory, that is, taking steps to design all public digital services in accordance with the W3C accessibility specifications.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million for a programme to be implemented by 'Clean Sri Lanka' to ensure physical accessibility within government institutions giving effect to a Supreme Court order and addressing the mobility needs of the elderly and persons with disabilities in the\n\n385 386\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\ncountry. Furthermore, it is ensured that provisions will be made available to every institution that requests such support.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 100 million has been allocated to develop the \u201cPannala Welcome Village\u201d elders' home under the National Secretariat for Elders as a model elderly care centre.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 75 million has been allocated for the construction of four new wards and a wastewater management system for homeless and destitute persons at the Rediyagama Kalana Detention Home.\n\n\u2022 Day care centres will be constructed for children with disabilities, and Rs. 200 million has been allocated to provide transport facilities for children with disabilities.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 100 million to extend State patronage for meeting the basic needs of care centres for persons with disabilities run by non-governmental organizations.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 500 million to provide facilities for high-capacity children's homes.\n\nSri Lankans Overseas"
