    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Rs. 400 million has been allocated to implement widely within the country the biological Wolbachia dengue vector control method with the technical contribution of the World Mosquito Programme - WMP - and the co-financing contribution of the Government, to control the dengue epidemic.\n\n\u2022 In addition to the development projects currently being implemented in hospitals providing secondary and tertiary care services, Rs. 1,245 million has been allocated to commence a number of new projects, including official quarters, at the Badulla and Batticaloa Teaching Hospitals, the\n\nMatale and Nawalapitiya District General Hospitals and the Puttalam Base Hospital.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 510 million has been allocated to prepare, in 2027, feasibility studies and preliminary plans relating to the identified development projects in hospitals, including the Matara District General Hospital, its relocation to the Kotawila area in Kamburugamuwa, the Kurunegala, Kalubowila and Kuliyapitiya Teaching Hospitals, the Trincomalee Siddha Teaching Hospital, the Moneragala and Polonnaruwa District General Hospitals, the National Institute of Infectious Diseases and the Gampola Base Hospital, as well as to providing accommodation facilities for hospital staff and establishing regional medical supplies stores as required.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to establish a centre within the Faculty of Medicine, Ragama to train doctors in Robotic Surgery. It is expected to provide training for the work of this centre in collaboration with foreign universities. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 250 million for this purpose."
