    "chunk_size_bytes": 1695,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 500 million to develop the Indian-assisted trilingual school premises in Polonnaruwa into a hotel school, including trilingual teaching, and to develop the Pinnawala Hotel School.\n\n\u2022 It is expected to deploy Rs. 500 million from the funds of the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau - SLTPB - for a concessionary loan scheme for tourism service providers to obtain the necessary equipment, including boats, to promote marine tourism.\n\n\u2022 A cruise tourism passenger terminal will be established in the Port of Colombo. Financing of Rs. 240 million will be provided from the funds of the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority - SLTDA - to modernize passenger terminal service facilities in the areas of Galle, Tangalle and Trincomalee and to expand the services provided to tourists.\n\n\u2022 It is expected to further strengthen the Tourist Police service to promote Sri Lanka as a safe tourist destination. It is proposed to provide a prompt and efficient security service to tourists by providing specialized training, deploying officers with multilingual capabilities, establishing special patrol units around major tourist sites, and introducing a 24-hour tourist emergency hotline service and a mobile application.\n\n24. Environmental Management\n\nIt is our duty to safeguard environmental balance for sustainable economic development. It is one of our fundamental responsibilities to secure the natural resources of the country for future generations by facing the challenges of climate change, protecting biodiversity and moving towards a green economy approach.\n\n\u2022 Our Government, which has understood the importance of the wildlife sector, has recruited"
