    "md5": "e213d903146bd4a4f6f9c9fbe1a1df6c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1630,
    "chunk_text": "It is our duty to safeguard environmental balance for sustainable economic development. It is one of our fundamental responsibilities to secure the natural resources of the country for future generations by facing the challenges of climate change, protecting biodiversity and moving towards a green economy approach.\n\n\u2022 Our Government, which has understood the importance of the wildlife sector, has recruited\n\n\u2022 With the aim of minimizing the human-elephant conflict and protecting human lives and wild elephants, the Handapanagala, Koholankala and Wetahira Kanda elephant corridors were released in June, 2026, and it is expected to declare the elephant corridor located between the Nachchaduwa Wewa and Maha Kanadarawa Wewa as a wildlife reserve.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 250 million has been allocated for the construction of new electric fences and the rehabilitation of existing electric fences. In addition, it is expected to allocate provisions of Rs. 200 million for this purpose from the Wildlife Fund as well.\n\n\u2022 A pilot project has been launched using artificial intelligence - AI - and thermal cameras to minimize accidents caused by wild elephants colliding with trains. Accordingly, it has been possible to reduce the number of such deaths this year. Based on its results, it is expected to implement this project nationally.\n\n\u2022 A land area of three acres has been identified within the Nuwaragam Forest Reserve in the Anuradhapura District to construct a hospital capable of treating wild animals for animal welfare. It is expected to allocate Rs. 700 million from the Wildlife Fund for the establishment of this hospital."
  },
