    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to amend the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance to increase, in addition to the existing term of imprisonment, the fine for killing, hunting, shooting, wounding or capturing a wild elephant from the current fine of Rs. 150,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 1 million. It is proposed to amend the Increase of Fines Act, No. 12 of 2005 to increase the fine for illegally keeping an elephant in possession from the current Rs. 150,000 to Rs. 250,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 1 million.\n\n\u2022 In addition to the above provisions, it is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million as advance preparedness to meet the requirements that may arise from the El Ni\u00f1o risk expected in the future.\n\n\u2022 Provisions have already been allocated to obtain vessels and machinery worth Rs. 3,380 million under Japanese cooperation to strengthen the capacity to respond promptly to marine and coastal pollution caused by oil spills, in order to protect the environment of the coastal belt.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 800 million has been allocated for 10 new sustainable environmental management projects, including the protection and stability of the eastern coastal belt, coastal protection in the Karukupane area in the Puttalam District, and the establishment of an ambient air quality monitoring network.\n\n\u2022 The protection of the central highlands, which are under severe threat, is the protection of the future of our nation. For this, it is proposed to establish an Upper Watershed Area Management Authority to establish an integrated watershed management approach and for restoration activities. It is expected to present the relevant Act to Parliament very soon. Discussions have already commenced to obtain loan assistance of US Dollars 100 million for the functions to be assigned to this Authority.\n\n7. Transport"
