    "chunk_size_bytes": 2021,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 The protection of the central highlands, which are under severe threat, is the protection of the future of our nation. For this, it is proposed to establish an Upper Watershed Area Management Authority to establish an integrated watershed management approach and for restoration activities. It is expected to present the relevant Act to Parliament very soon. Discussions have already commenced to obtain loan assistance of US Dollars 100 million for the functions to be assigned to this Authority.\n\n7. Transport\n\nmodernizing railway and passenger bus services, strengthening connectivity between transport networks and promoting sustainable public transport.\n\n\u2022 It is expected to extend the Metro Bus service introduced around Colombo this year to the urban areas of Kandy, Galle and Jaffna as well.\n\n\u2022 The Government has invested in Metro Buses up to now. More than 120 buses are already in operation. A further 50 buses are scheduled to be added to that company in 2027. In addition, we have also planned to introduce electric buses. One hundred buses are scheduled to be received for this purpose as a donation from the Government of China. Activities such as the construction of the depots required for these buses, the provision of the necessary charging facilities and the provision of training will commence next year, and provisions of Rs. 4,500 million have been allocated for this purpose.\n\n\u2022 To encourage the private sector to deploy Metro Buses as well, existing route permit holders will be encouraged to add a modern low-floor bus to operation in place of their existing buses.\n\n\u2022 Steps have already been taken to import 600 air-conditioned buses to provide a comfortable and safe service to long-distance passengers.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to purchase 50 small buses with 22 seats required for rural areas with narrow hill roads.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 4,000 million to obtain 200 small buses with 33 seats required for passenger services in rural areas."
