    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to purchase 50 small buses with 22 seats required for rural areas with narrow hill roads.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 4,000 million to obtain 200 small buses with 33 seats required for passenger services in rural areas.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 600 million to establish the Department of Motor Traffic on the Werahera premises in order to provide a more efficient service.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 700 million has been allocated to establish a modern digital system for the process of vehicle registration and transfer of ownership, with the aim of providing efficient and transparent services to the public.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,500 million has been allocated to establish a new digital Driver Demerit Points System and a road safety enforcement system, integrating the Department of Motor Traffic and the Sri Lanka Police, to minimize road accidents and for road safety.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated to purchase five new trains for the railway service.\n\n\u2022 Provisions of Rs. 2,000 million have been allocated in 2027 for the programme to repair railway stations that have not been properly maintained for a long time.\n\n393 394\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n\u2022 Train operations between Colombo and Peradeniya have been resumed by deploying the resources of the Department of Railways with maximum efficiency to restore the up-country railway line damaged by the Ditwah disaster.\n\n\u2022 Under the Government of India loan assistance programme, the work required to rehabilitate the railway section from Rambukkana to Peradeniya, the up-country railway line from Peradeniya to Gampola, and the Matale railway line in a safer and more stable manner, in accordance with modern engineering standards, has commenced. It is expected that trains will be able to operate up to Kandy within the first quarter of 2027.\n\n\u2022 Accordingly, it is expected to fully rehabilitate the Up-Country railway line and restore train operations up to Badulla by the middle of 2027."
