    "md5": "ea0ef2f29e5f6bb4b5cfde6fa1793625",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "A secure house and a healthy urban environment are the most fundamental basis for the progress of a nation and its human resources. Our expectation is to uplift the living standards of the people by planning economic, social and physical development in an integrated manner, while protecting the natural and built environment.\n\n395 396\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\n\u2022 Thirteen thousand families displaced due to the armed conflict that prevailed in the North and the East have still not been resettled. It is the target of our Government to complete the resettlement of these families within two years. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated for this purpose, and it is proposed to allocate a further Rs. 4,000 million.\n\n\u2022 The programme to construct 10,000 houses, launched with the cooperation of the Government of India to resolve the housing problem of the plantation community will be further accelerated.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate a provision of Rs. 1,000 million for providing houses to those in areas such as Abaranchimulla, Serakkuliya, Mangalapura, Kandasamy Nagar and Nithya Nagar in Vavuniya, Pediyafarm, Polonnaruwa, Mullaitivu, Tissamaharama, Divulapitiya, Dimbulagala and Hennanigala-South who were affected by the Ditwah disaster but did not become entitled to a house due to the existing criteria.\n\n\u2022 The owners of a large number of housing projects, which were commenced in the years 2015 - 2019 with small financial assistance of Rs. 20,000 and Rs. 40,000 and were abandoned midway, have been put to great hardship. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 5,000 million for financial assistance of up to Rs. 500,000 to eligible beneficiaries to complete the remaining construction work of half-completed houses.\n\n\u2022 It is expected to allocate Rs. 90,000 million through the Supplementary Estimate for the construction of houses under the Ditwah Housing Project."
