    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 200 million for feasibility studies and the preparation of plans to construct a new administrative building to house in a single building the various divisions of the Sri Lanka Police Department, which are currently operating in buildings obtained on a rental basis at various locations in the City of Colombo, with the aim of providing a more efficient service to the public.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to provide police officers in June, 2027 with a new uniform suited to the climatic conditions of our country and equipped with modern technological devices.\n\n\u2022 Rehabilitating persons addicted to dangerous drugs and reintegrating them into society is a long-term and important objective of the \"Ratama Ekata\" National Operation. For this, Rs. 180 million has been allocated for the development of infrastructure at the Senapura and Kandakadu rehabilitation centres and the full development of counselling and treatment services and vocational training facilities.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 6,200 million has been allocated for activities including ensuring border security in line with national and international policies and standards on immigration and emigration, developing the Wattala Temporary Detention Centre with facilities conforming to international standards for foreigners temporarily detained due to visa crises and complications, establishing a new office complex in Trincomalee to enhance regional operations, and digitalizing immigration and emigration activities.\n\n\u2022 Legislative work has already commenced to grant permanent residency to investors based on the size of the investment and other relevant criteria.\n\n29. Judiciary"
