    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Rs. 6,200 million has been allocated for activities including ensuring border security in line with national and international policies and standards on immigration and emigration, developing the Wattala Temporary Detention Centre with facilities conforming to international standards for foreigners temporarily detained due to visa crises and complications, establishing a new office complex in Trincomalee to enhance regional operations, and digitalizing immigration and emigration activities.\n\n\u2022 Legislative work has already commenced to grant permanent residency to investors based on the size of the investment and other relevant criteria.\n\n29. Judiciary\n\n\u2022 Rs. 5,115 million has been allocated for the expansion and development of facilities in the existing courts in Jaffna, Batticaloa, Trincomalee, Mannar, Nuwara Eliya, Kegalle, Gampaha, Kalutara, Kandy and Colombo.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 60 million has been allocated for the complete digitalization of the activities of the Government Analyst's Department.\n\n\u2022 The Supreme Court e-filing portal, the capacity for paperless hearings, integrated case management and online payments - e-CMS - have already been implemented as components of the programme to obtain the support of digitalization for the efficiency of the judicial system. The implementation of this programme within the Supreme Court has now been completed, and the process for its implementation in other courts has commenced.\n\nSevere congestion has arisen within the prison system of our country. Exceeding the capacity to hold around 16,500 persons in 22 prisons and 14 work camps, nearly 36,500 inmates, around twice that number, are currently being held. Officers as well as inmates have lost their lives due to unfortunate incidents that occurred within prisons as a result of this congestion and the drug menace.\n\n399 400\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc 