    "chunk_size_bytes": 1574,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 As a tribute to the parents of war heroes who joined the armed forces before 2009, it is proposed that the Ministry of Defence expeditiously prepare a programme to increase the monthly allowance of Rs. 750 currently paid to the mother and father and to implement it from July, 2027.\n\n\u2022 Steps will be taken to modernize the digital and cybersecurity systems of the Ministry of Defence, establish a digital forensic laboratory and develop border security technological facilities. It is also expected to improve the communication and technological facilities of the Sri Lanka Army, and to provide new patrol craft, tug boats and modern radar systems to strengthen the maritime security and surveillance capabilities of the Sri Lanka Navy.\n\n31. Cultural and National Heritage\n\nOur national identity has been established through all ethnicities and religions living in harmony as one family. It is one of our foremost responsibilities to formally conserve that heritage in order to bequeath it to future generations.\n\nFor this, steps will be taken to digitalize and conserve sacred places, historical artefacts and cultural identities through digital technological innovations such as 3D laser scanning used internationally as well as locally. This will make it possible to permanently maintain accurate three-dimensional models of the national heritage even in the face of natural disasters or weather impacts.\n\nRs. 7,000 million has been allocated in this Budget for the promotion and development of artistic activities associated with various ethnicities and religions."
