    "md5": "efad7d10d0a09c3b7d62f2a79dc25947",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1766,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Provisions have been allocated amounting to Rs. 400 million to the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation and Rs. 489 million to the Independent TelevisionNetwork, for implementing digitalization activities, improving broadcasting facilities and purchasing modern equipment and technological tools. Rs. 384 million has been allocated to the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation for Recurrent Expenditure.\n\n33. Clean Sri Lanka\n\n\u2022 The Clean Sri Lanka programme aims to transform Sri Lankan life, extending well beyond mere physical cleanliness, by steering it toward a positive direction in social, environmental and ethical terms. Under its social pillar, the programme seeks to strengthen quality of life, dignity, safety, equal access, inclusivity, community participation and social harmony; under its environmental pillar, it focuses on promoting environmental protection, conservation, stewardship, biodiversity, responsible resource utilization and sustainability and under its ethical pillar, it seeks to strengthen responsibility, honesty, discipline, fairness, efficiency and accountability regarding public resources. Rs. 6,000 million has been allocated to implement these programmes.\n\n\u2022 Various programmes are being implemented, including: the provision and sustainable maintenance of physical infrastructure, such as \u201cHaritha Mawatha,\u201d \u201cClean Colombo,\u201d \u201cClean Islands,\u201d \u201cClean City,\u201d \u201cClean Sri Lanka-Aththama,\u201d the modernization of 'Dream Destination' railway stations, and the establishment of standardized public sanitation facilities; environmental development projects, including the creation of elephant nourishment zones; and initiatives to promote positive public habits, community participation, and corporate responsibility."
