    "md5": "8ceccd2b4a1b57eb6d6841fe86f7206a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1885,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, through our first Budget in 2025, steps were taken to increase the basic salary by increasing the minimum monthly basic salary of the public sector by Rs. 15,750 and by increasing the value of the annual salary\n\nMeanwhile, public servants in various sectors have submitted requests to revise their allowances, considering the increase in the related expenses they have to bear in the performance of their duties. Taking into account those requests as well as the fiscal space currently available to the Government, we expect to increase several allowances on a priority basis through this Budget. Requests to revise other allowances will be considered in phases in future Budgets, taking into account the fiscal capacity of the Government.\n\nAccordingly, it is proposed to revise allowances as follows.\n\nTransport Allowance of Executive Officers in the Public Service\n\n\u2022 Executive officers who are entitled to an official vehicle under Public Administration Circular No. 05/2016 but use their private vehicles in the performance of official duties are currently paid a monthly transport allowance of Rs. 50,000. Considering the increase in maintenance, repair and other operational costs when private vehicles are used for official duties, and since it is more cost-effective for the Government to allow officers who own a vehicle to use their private vehicle rather than being provided with a Government vehicle, in order to encourage this, it is proposed to increase the monthly transport allowance currently paid to Rs. 100,000.\n\n\u2022 With the aim of encouraging the use of electric vehicles, it is proposed to increase by 150 per cent, with effect from July, 2027, the monthly allowance paid in terms of Public Administration Circular 13/2008(V) to officers entitled to an official vehicle and who use fully electric private vehicles.\n\nAllowances in the Health Sector"
  },
