    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Likewise, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 2,250 currently paid to civil officers serving in the Department of Prisons to Rs. 10,000.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to pay these proposed allowances of officers serving in the Department of Prisons with effect from July, 2027.\n\nAllowances for Field Officers\n\n\u2022 The monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Development Officers will be increased from Rs. 300 to Rs. 1,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 1,000 to Rs. 2,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 750 to Rs. 1,500 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\n\u2022 The monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Samurdhi Officers will be increased from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 2,500, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 2,500 to Rs. 5,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to increase the monthly travelling allowance currently paid to Agriculture Research and Production Assistants from Rs. 400 to Rs. 1,000, and the monthly office rent allowance from Rs. 3,000 to Rs. 6,000 for Municipal Council and Urban Council areas and from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000 for Pradeshiya Sabha areas.\n\n\u2022 The above allowances for field officers will be revised from April 2027.\n\nRevision of Allowances in the Judicial Sector\n\nAllowances of High Court Judges and Judicial Officers\n\n\u2022 Considering the professional responsibilities, the nature of service and the role of officers in the judicial sector, it is proposed to increase by Rs. 25,000 the monthly professional allowance currently paid to High Court Judges, Special Grade Judicial Officers and Judicial Officers of other grades. Steps will be taken to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n407 408\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc 