    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Considering the professional responsibilities, the nature of service and the role of officers in the judicial sector, it is proposed to increase by Rs. 25,000 the monthly professional allowance currently paid to High Court Judges, Special Grade Judicial Officers and Judicial Officers of other grades. Steps will be taken to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n407 408\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\nAllowances of the Attorney-General's Department\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to increase the monthly non-practising allowance by Rs. 25,000 for the posts of Attorney-General, Solicitor General and Senior State Counsel, and by Rs. 20,000 for officers in the posts of Senior State Attorney and State Attorney of the Attorney-General's Department. Steps will be taken to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July, 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n\u2022 With effect from July, 2027, it is proposed to increase the monthly transport allowance paid to officers entitled to official vehicles by Rs. 50,000, the monthly driver allowance paid to entitled officers from Rs. 25,000 to Rs. 50,000, and the housing allowance currently paid by 100 per cent.\n\nAllowances of the Legal Draftsman's Department\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to increase the special allowance of officers in the posts of Legal Draftsman, Additional Legal Draftsman and Deputy Legal Draftsman of the Legal Draftsman's Department by Rs. 25,000, and the special allowance of Senior Assistant Legal Draftsmen and Assistant Legal Draftsmen by Rs. 20,000. Steps will be taken to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n\u2022 With effect from July 2027, the monthly driver allowance paid to entitled officers will be increased from Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 50,000.\n\nAllowances of Judicial Support Staff"
