    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to increase the special allowance of officers in the posts of Legal Draftsman, Additional Legal Draftsman and Deputy Legal Draftsman of the Legal Draftsman's Department by Rs. 25,000, and the special allowance of Senior Assistant Legal Draftsmen and Assistant Legal Draftsmen by Rs. 20,000. Steps will be taken to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n\u2022 With effect from July 2027, the monthly driver allowance paid to entitled officers will be increased from Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 50,000.\n\nAllowances of Judicial Support Staff\n\nMonthly Allowances of Independent Commissions, Other Commissions and Statutory Institutions\n\n\u2022 As the monthly allowances of the Chairpersons and members of Independent Commissions and other Commissions have not been revised since 2018, and the monthly allowances of the Chairpersons, Executive Directors and Working Directors of State Corporations, Statutory Institutions and Government-owned companies have not been increased since 2015, it is proposed to increase their monthly allowances with effect from July, 2027, taking into account the responsibilities they hold.\n\n\u2022 The monthly allowances paid to the Chairpersons and members of other Commissions will be revised as per Annexure VI.\n\nHon. Speaker, Further details on the revision of the above allowances are included in the Technical Note.\n\nRevision of Public Service Pensions\n\nHon. Speaker,\n\nPension Revision and Relief to Pensioners\n\n\u2022 The Government is implementing a phased pension revision programme with the objective of ensuring a fair and structured pension system for all pensioners by systematically eliminating the disparities that exist among the pensions of retired public servants."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
