    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "f347679eb62787ab602bb7924e3e68ce",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 The overall objective of all these measures is to provide fair relief to public servants who retired at different times by systematically narrowing the pension disparities among them, and to establish a sustainable pension system in the long term.\n\n36. Tax Policy Proposals\n\n36.1 Increasing the Personal Income Tax Relief\n\nand Revising the Progressive Tax Slabs\n\nTo provide further relief to personal income taxpayers, it is proposed to further increase the annual Personal Income Tax free threshold and to revise the Personal Income Tax structure by expanding the taxable income brackets.\n\nWe were able to increase the tax-free threshold from Rs. 100,000 per month to Rs. 150,000. Through the proposed revisions, it will be further increased to Rs. 162,500. Accordingly, a person receiving a monthly salary and allowances of up to Rs. 162,500 will not be required to pay tax on his or her salary.\n\nThe tax slab to which the 6 per cent tax rate applies will be Rs. 70,833 per month, and thereafter the tax slabs will be widened from Rs. 41,667 per month to Rs. 50,000 per month. The tax rates will be set at 6 per cent, 12 per cent, 18 percent, 24 per cent, 30 per cent and 36 per cent, applying a rate of 12 per cent instead of 18 per cent after the 6 percent rate.\n\nThese revisions will raise the monthly income threshold at which the maximum Personal Income Tax rate applies from Rs. 358,000 to Rs. 433,000. Consequently, each individual taxpayer will receive an additional monthly tax relief ranging from a minimum of Rs. 750 to a maximum of Rs. 15,750.\n\nAccordingly, as a combined result of the tax reforms introduced in 2025 and the revisions proposed for 2027, the total monthly tax relief provided by our Government to each individual taxpayer will increase ranging from a minimum of Rs. 4,250 to a maximum of Rs. 36,250.\n\n36.2 Enhanced Capital Allowances for Export-Oriented Manufacturing and Tourism Businesses Approved by the Board of Investment (BOI)"
  },
  {
