    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "30e6defa22e60a5eb069b457bc856963",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1789,
    "chunk_text": "Accordingly, as a combined result of the tax reforms introduced in 2025 and the revisions proposed for 2027, the total monthly tax relief provided by our Government to each individual taxpayer will increase ranging from a minimum of Rs. 4,250 to a maximum of Rs. 36,250.\n\n36.2 Enhanced Capital Allowances for Export-Oriented Manufacturing and Tourism Businesses Approved by the Board of Investment (BOI)\n\nAccordingly, BOI-approved enterprises engaged in export-oriented manufacturing or tourism development activities with a minimum qualifying investment of US Dollars 3 million will be permitted subject to meeting the relevant requirements to opt for an enhanced capital allowance equivalent to 200 per cent of qualifying capital expenditure in place of the existing allowance regime.\n\n36.3 Exemption of Exercise Books and Printed Books from Value Added Tax \u2013VAT\n\nHon. Speaker, printed books and other printed materials became subject to Value Added Tax \u2013 VAT - effective from January 2024, while exercise books had been subject to VAT even before that date.\n\nRecognizing the importance of education and the necessity of ensuring that essential educational materials are available at an affordable price, and with the objective of promoting access to education, knowledge and reading, we propose to exempt textbooks, dictionaries, encyclopaedias, children's drawing and colouring books, educational publications and other printed books, as well as exercise books, from Value Added Tax -VAT.\n\n36.4 Revising the Basis for Calculating VAT\n\nLiability on Cinema Ticket Revenue\n\nWith the aim of ensuring the fair and equitable application of Value Added Tax within the film industry, we propose to revise the basis for calculating the VAT liability arising from the sale of cinema tickets."
