    "md5": "5208952e6a78e63148771312e0ce0350",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1855,
    "chunk_text": "With the aim of ensuring the fair and equitable application of Value Added Tax within the film industry, we propose to revise the basis for calculating the VAT liability arising from the sale of cinema tickets.\n\n36.5 Facilitating Earlier Qualification of Newly VAT Registered Exporters as \u201cEligible Exporters\u201d\n\nHon. Speaker, with the aim of facilitating export-oriented businesses, I propose to revise the criteria under which newly VAT registered exporters are recognized as Eligible Exporters.\n\nAccordingly, newly VAT registered persons will be recognized as Eligible Exporters where more than 80 per cent of their turnover during the preceding six months has\n\n411 412\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\nbeen derived from exports, without having to satisfy the existing requirement relating to the preceding calendar year.\n\n36.6 Use of the Indicative Exchange Rate of the\n\nCentral Bank of Sri Lanka for Value Added Tax on Foreign Currency Supplies\n\nHon. Speaker, in order to ensure greater transparency, consistency and fairness in valuing taxable supplies denominated in foreign currencies, it is proposed to use the Indicative Exchange Rate published by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka for the conversion of foreign currencies into Sri Lanka Rupees for VAT purposes. The Commissioner General of Inland Revenue \u2013CGIR- will specify by way of a circular the manner in which such exchange rate is to be applied.\n\n36.7 Social Security Contribution Levy \u2013SSCL -\n\nExemption for Bunker Fuel, Supplied to Ships Engaged in International Transportation\n\nHon. Speaker, the supply of bunker fuel to ships engaged in international transport is an important component of Sri Lanka's maritime services sector. This industry operates in a highly competitive international market."
  },
