    "date_str": "2026-11-12",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-11-12",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24650_english_2026-11-12.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-12-2026-11-12-0496",
    "chunk_index": 496,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "513e06a71ce5be637eb8ebff8ec8ad1c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1787,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, what we must leave behind for future generations is not our party disputes, but a prosperous and just country the future of which they can take over with confidence. Therefore, let us make the name \"Sri Lankan\" not merely a name we pronounce with pride, but a proud name that the whole world accepts with respect.\n\nToday, we extend an invitation with an open heart to all political parties in this country, to all stakeholders, and to every Sri Lankan living anywhere in the world. Come, let us become partners in building the future of this\n\ncountry! We do not need to think along the same lines; we do not need to hold the same opinion. But our country is greater than our differences. The future of our children is more valuable than our individual goals. Therefore, let us bring together our knowledge, our abilities and our strengths. Let us begin from where we can agree. Let us unite, not to get ahead of one another, but to take our Motherland ahead of us all!\n\nIn the end, what we must leave behind for our children is not the story of how far above one another we stood, but the story of how high we all, together, raised this country.\n\nThe victory of that story will not belong to one individual; it will not belong to one party; it will not belong to one generation alone.\n\nThat victory will belong to every citizen of this country. That victory must have only one name \u2013 Sri Lanka!\n\nFinally, I express my sincere gratitude to all the officials of the Ministry of Finance and the Secretary to the Treasury, Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, who worked with unwavering dedication and perseverance in preparing this Budget. Their professionalism, dedication and sense of duty have been instrumental in the preparation of this comprehensive and forward-looking Budget."
  },
