    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca \u0da2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0da0\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dba\u0da0\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb1\u0b9c\u0bc0\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0bc6\u0baf\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf)\u0baf\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf) (The Hon. Rajeevan Jeyachandramoorthy) Hon. Speaker, through my first Supplementary Question, I wish to raise several concerns regarding the management and the deployment of Teacher Educators in National Colleges of Education and Teacher Development Centres. There are reports of serious shortcomings in staff deployment, institutional management, infrastructure and career progression. In particular, the Vavuniya National College of Education reportedly has three Art Teacher Educators despite it not offering Art as a subject. Similarly, a Drama and Theatre Teacher Educator is serving in another institution where the subject is not offered.\n\nSeveral centres reportedly operate without clear annual programmes and measurable targets of effective performance monitoring. Also, some institutions with an approved cadre of four reportedly have more than ten staff members, creating unnecessary expenditure of public funds. Residential facilities have not been upgraded for decades. So, Teacher Educators are compelled to stay in deteriorating quarters, while eight to ten student teachers sometimes share a single room.\n\nMillions of rupees allocated to these institutions are reportedly returned to the Treasury annually without being utilized. Then, there are concerns about the absence of a transparent and consistent transfer policy. Also, the Teacher Educators reportedly have to wait approximately for 18 years to reach Grade I.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) Hon. Member, you have to shorten your Question."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-2026-11-13",
    "num": "2026-11-13",
