    "description": "Hansard of 2026-11-13",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24659_english_2026-11-13.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-13-2026-11-13-0017",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "cb46e5e264b8d255d64dde08c1db0dc7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2138,
    "chunk_text": "Millions of rupees allocated to these institutions are reportedly returned to the Treasury annually without being utilized. Then, there are concerns about the absence of a transparent and consistent transfer policy. Also, the Teacher Educators reportedly have to wait approximately for 18 years to reach Grade I.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) Hon. Member, you have to shorten your Question.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0baf) \u0bbf\u0baf) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harini Amarasuriya) Sir, it is correct that the National Colleges of Education are not at an acceptable level. For many years, those Colleges of Education have been neglected. Staff have not been recruited; the cadre has not been filled and infrastructure development has not taken place. And, we are gradually addressing all of those issues.\n\nThe main issue was the large number of vacancies that have been existing since 2019, which we started filling this year. In addition to the 600 odd staff recruited on a limited basis, a further 200-plus were recently recruited on an open basis as well. So, gradually, the staff requirement is being met.\n\nIn parallel, infrastructure development is taking place in the Colleges of Education. Money has been allocated. As far as I know, the infrastructure development that we have planned for 2025/2026 is taking place. From 2027 onwards, the allocation for the development of National Colleges of Education will also increase because, from 2027, we are prioritizing the development of National Colleges of Education.\n\nIn addition, for the first time, they are also being connected to the Internet, and digital education teaching facilities are being provided. We have already started a digital education hub at the Maharagama National College of Education, which is connected with five other National Colleges of Education. So, all these are currently being implemented."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-13-2026-11-13",
