    "chunk_size_bytes": 2009,
    "chunk_text": "Aswesuma is the Government\u2019s main cash-transfer programme for low-income families. Of the Rs. 231 billion allocated in 2026 for Aswesuma and other household cash grants, Rs, 89.6 billion or 38.8 per cent was spent in the first six months.\n\nAccordingly, as a matter of urgent public importance, I request the Hon. Minister to clarify the following:\n\n1. Which five Ministries recorded the lowest utilization of their 2026 capital allocations as at 30th June, 2026?\n\nAt the Committee Stage, we are going to have Discussions on how much has been allocated to each Ministry. But, we are going to have the Discussions without knowing last year\u2019s expenditure, how much the Ministries have spent and so on.\n\n2. What were the main reasons reported by Ministries for the low utilization of capital allocations between January-June, 2026?\n\nWe are not asking for figures up until October, 2026 because we understand that that quarter had just ended. So, what we are asking is to, at least, go by the basis of the first six months.\n\n3. What was the value of bills for completed works received by the Ministry of Finance from other Ministries, but not yet paid as at 30th June, 2026?\n\n4. Will any unspent 2026 capital allocation be reallocated by the Ministry of Finance to other purposes before 31st December, 2026, and if so, to which purposes?\n\nWe saw the Hon. President yesterday boasting about a Budget surplus. Sir, I understand keeping some money as a contingency fund. But, if we have excessive money, will we be spending it before the end of the year?\n\n5. Will the Government use the unspent balance of the\n\nRs. 231 billion cash-grant allocation to increase Aswesuma coverage or benefit amounts before the end of 2026?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2 \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca \u0db8\u0dd3\u0da7 \u0db4\u0dd9\u0dbb \u0dbb \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dda \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dca\u0db1\u0dba \u0d85\u0dc4\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0db6\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf. \u0db1\u0db8\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca, \u0d85\u0daf \u0d85\u0daf"
