    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b6e7b9bd05d073b1b5157610b4104635",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0d92 \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0dda\u0db8 \u0dad\u0dc0 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dab\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca \u0db8 \u0dad\u0dc0 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dab\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca \u0db8\u0db8 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1 \u0d95\u0db1\u0dd1. Sir, another important matter that I must raise is this. Generally, a Budget Speech is the policy direction of the Government for the next year. The Budget Speech is not only a statement of the country's fiscal position or the economic position, but also the country's or the Government's plan or what the Government plans to do in the following year. That is a policy statement.\n\nThere should have been a mention of accountability and the justice mechanism. The Hon. Minister of Justice and National Integration is here. I acknowledge, Hon. Minister, that you have almost doubled the budgetary allocations for the Office on Missing Persons and the Office for Reparations, but the domestic mechanism proposed is a mechanism that the victim community has rejected. So, you are allocating money to a mechanism, of which the victim community is not going to be part. Therefore, I do not know who justice is going to be for.\n\nPrevious Governments, in their policy statements, would mention the Provincial Council Elections. But, this time, not a single word about the Provincial Council Elections, Sir! About the Provincial Council Elections, what have you all mentioned? You are taking away the powers of Provincial Councils. By bringing six District\n\nGeneral Hospitals - the District Hospitals of Mullaitivu, Mannar, Kilinochchi, Vavuniya, Avissawella and Gampaha - under the Central Government, you are taking away the powers given to the Provincial Councils whilst not holding the Provincial Council Elections. Last year, the powers given to the provinces under environmental policies, you had taken back without the consent of the provincial councils. Then, about land release, not a word, Sir!"
  },
  {
