    "md5": "5954b557e96b9aaf4c2db8402910c95a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1295,
    "chunk_text": "Crucially, Madam, look at how this Budget raises revenue. For years, the answer to every fiscal shortfall was to squeeze the salaried worker and the compliant taxpayer even harder, while tax evaders walked free. This Budget flips this approach on its head. By upgrading to RAMIS 3, which we have already done, introducing real-time API-based e-invoicing and implementing a data-driven, risk-based tax audit system, we are closing loopholes and removing human discretion - and, therefore, corruption - from tax administration. When everyone pays their fair share, no single citizen is crushed under an unfair burden.\n\nEven more importantly, we have addressed the single biggest obstacle facing our small and medium enterprises: access to affordable credit. With over Rs. 174 billion dedicated to SME development including concessional loans at 3 per cent interest, targeted support for women-headed household, export-oriented enterprises and the operationalization of the National Credit Guarantee Institution, a young entrepreneur with a viable business plan no longer needs massive collateral or political patronage to get started. Combined with our simplified National Tariff Policy and the Trade National Single Window, we are making it easier to produce in Sri Lanka and export to the world."
