    "chunk_index": 127,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "348b1537cdb4239946aca8ce35f07eb8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1841,
    "chunk_text": "Even more importantly, we have addressed the single biggest obstacle facing our small and medium enterprises: access to affordable credit. With over Rs. 174 billion dedicated to SME development including concessional loans at 3 per cent interest, targeted support for women-headed household, export-oriented enterprises and the operationalization of the National Credit Guarantee Institution, a young entrepreneur with a viable business plan no longer needs massive collateral or political patronage to get started. Combined with our simplified National Tariff Policy and the Trade National Single Window, we are making it easier to produce in Sri Lanka and export to the world.\n\nAt the same time, we have not forgotten the backbone of our real economy: our farmers, our rural communities and our physical infrastructure. A staggering Rs. 91.7 billion has been allocated to restore our historic irrigation networks, including giants like the Senanayake Samudraya and Gal Oya. When we invest in irrigation, we invest in food security and rural dignity. Alongside\n\n527 528\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nthis, Rs. 58.2 billion for expressways, rural roads and bridges, plus Rs. 6.9 billion for 600 new SLTB buses and modern railway units will ensure that goods move efficiently from the farm gate to the port and the working people commute with dignity.\n\nFinally, Madam, let me speak about the moral heart of this Budget, how it treats the working people and the most vulnerable citizens of this country. Critics claimed that strict fiscal discipline w10ould mean abandoning the poor and freezing public wages. This Budget proves them wrong. We have allocated Rs. 130 billion towards revising public sector salaries and pensions, recognizing that an efficient, incorruptible Public Service must be fairly compensated."
