    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24659_english_2026-11-13.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-13-2026-11-13-0162",
    "chunk_index": 162,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "e3312b6144fa3c7c281e7b37b1a30ac5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1870,
    "chunk_text": "If one asks what this Budget is all about, we would say that it is about the industrial policy the Opposition could not implement over the last 30 years. For four decades, there was no industrial policy for the country. So, if you would really look at this entire Budget, it is about the industrial policy.\n\nAll these years, they ran the economy with twin deficits, a fiscal deficit and a foreign currency Current Account deficit. We have changed that. Now, there is no fiscal deficit or a foreign currency deficit. So, why are you shouting about a fear? The country is not going to fall in any way. Debt sustainability has been achieved; fiscal discipline has been maintained, and that is what we have been doing for the last two years. Now, we are moving on to the phase of growth.\n\nThe Opposition has to clearly say their stance on the IMF and the World Bank. You have to, because you are saying two things which nobody could understand. We have always been against those institutions because we have had bad experiences across the world. What we are now saying is that the country is dependent on those organizations because you all had not developed the nation. You had 30 to 40 years to do that. When the country is vulnerable, when the country is weak, you have to seek the support of those institutions. That is the reality, and we are facing that reality. We have come through that as well.\n\nThroughout the entire Budget Speech of the President, he clearly articulated how that growth is going to be achieved. But, the Opposition was not listening to it. I think the people who understand know that in that, we talk about reforms, the reforms that had never happened in this country before.\n\nThe rule of law, digitalization, the Public-Private Partnership Bill, the Tariff Policy, the State-Owned\n\n547 548\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
