    "chunk_index": 163,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ed5c8506bbaf56e147038ecc10a0674d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1944,
    "chunk_text": "Throughout the entire Budget Speech of the President, he clearly articulated how that growth is going to be achieved. But, the Opposition was not listening to it. I think the people who understand know that in that, we talk about reforms, the reforms that had never happened in this country before.\n\nThe rule of law, digitalization, the Public-Private Partnership Bill, the Tariff Policy, the State-Owned\n\n547 548\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nThen, infrastructure development. Without infrastructure development, no investment is going to come in. Why should investors come? The infrastructure development the previous Governments did was not useful. The Hambantota Port, the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport and the highway leading to that area were not priorities at that point of time. Instead, they should have built the Central Expressway. That is where production is happening; Kurunegala and Kandy will be our next industrial areas. So, you all should have done that. Now, we are doing it. We are ensuring that infrastructure is developed. All the ports are being developed, the transportation system is being developed, all the highways are being started and all the airports are going to be developed, including Ratmalana and Palaly Airports and the expansion of the Katunayake Airport. Those are infrastructure requirements for investors to come to this country.\n\nWhen it comes to market connectivity, you all said that some people were against the FTAs and all that proposed to be brought in. You all did not go into FTAs with feasibility studies and ensuring that the local industries are protected. Now, we have done all that and are ready to enter into FTAs. So, with those, this country will get connected to India, China, the Middle East, Africa and Europe. Therefore, those are the priorities of this Government. And, it is only when we give that direction, investments will start flowing in."
  },
