    "md5": "e41ebccaf9070a6ace01b08e96c07b5a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1142,
    "chunk_text": "When it comes to market connectivity, you all said that some people were against the FTAs and all that proposed to be brought in. You all did not go into FTAs with feasibility studies and ensuring that the local industries are protected. Now, we have done all that and are ready to enter into FTAs. So, with those, this country will get connected to India, China, the Middle East, Africa and Europe. Therefore, those are the priorities of this Government. And, it is only when we give that direction, investments will start flowing in.\n\nWith regard education reforms, we are 30 to 40 years behind. Where are the skills, the mindset and the capability required to enter into the modern job market? So, that is the change we are making to meet the inputs required for industrial growth.\n\nOn the other side, we are bringing in incentivization. We have that opportunity now because the IMF programme is coming to an end. We can provide incentives, prioritizing certain sectors. We are now going to introduce incentives for industries, which extend beyond the Western Province. The previous administrations had not been able to do so. Yes, I agree"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
