    "chunk_text": "This does not impose any legal restriction on them from practising treatments or using medicines specific to their own traditional or other indigenous systems of medicine. However, the manufacture of such unique indigenous treatments or medicines and their release to the market are not legally permissible under the existing law and this legal provision shall remain valid and continue to have effect in the future, as it does at present.\n\n(b) (i) Yes.\n\n(ii) The Ayurveda Medical Council registers traditional practitioners who have come through traditional/ Gurukula systems of training in accordance with Section 55(1) of the Ayurveda Act, No. 31 of 1961. In accordance with the Regulations formulated by the Ayurveda Medical Council under the provisions of the Act, a mechanism is maintained to conduct written and oral examinations to determine whether the relevant applicants have acquired knowledge, experience and skills required to practise Ayurveda medicine efficiently to the satisfaction of the Council and to register such applicants who pass the examinations.\n\nThe relevant student is supervised by the Guru Practitioner (the teacher). Furthermore, upon submission of the applications, the Ayurveda Community Medical Officer examines the information furnished by the applicants and submits a report thereon to the Provincial Commissioner of Ayurveda. Thereafter, an observation report is obtained by the Ayurveda Medical Council through the Provincial Commissioner of Ayurveda.\n\n(c) (i) No.\n\nIn terms of the Ayurveda Act, No. 31 of 1961 and the amendments thereto, the authority to register practitioners and regulate trainees is vested exclusively in the Ayurveda Medical Council. However, the Ayurveda Medical Council operates a supporting mechanism at the regional level through Ayurveda Community Medical Officers to obtain information.\n\n(ii) Does not arise.\n\n(d) Does not arise.\n\n827 828\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0daf\u0dbd\u0dd9\u0dba) \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd9 \u0dbd \u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dc0\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0ddc]\n\n\u0dd9\u0dd0.\u0dba\u0dd4."
